RUN

Runs at build time (when building the image).

Used to install things, copy, set up environment.

Each RUN creates a new image layer.

Example:

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y python3

▶️ CMD

Runs at container start (runtime).

Sets the default command if you don’t provide one.

Can be overridden when you run the container.

Example:

CMD ["python3", "app.py"]   # default command

🎯 ENTRYPOINT

Also runs at container start, but is harder to override.

Treat it as the main executable of the container.

You can still pass arguments (from CMD or docker run).

Example:

ENTRYPOINT ["python3"]
CMD ["app.py"]   # becomes: python3 app.py
